{
  "name": "Telecom Churn Retention",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": ["## Telecom churn retention\n\nSame path as the Streamlit Action Center.\n\n**Score with XGBoost** runs `src/batch_score.py`. That script loads `models/model.joblib` and `models/preprocessor.joblib`, drops `customerID` and `Churn`, coerces blank `TotalCharges`, and scores with `predict_proba` on the churn class. Top risk factors are the three largest positive contributions (`transformed value × feature importance`), with `_` rewritten as `: `.\n\n",
          "**High Churn Risk?** follows `high_threshold = 70` in `streamlit/tab_action.py`. The true branch also requires `already_churned` to be false, so a historical `Churn = Yes` row does not get a retention draft. Everyone else lands on **Safe Retention Level**.\n\n**Draft Retention Email** calls Claude `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` (`max_tokens` 400, `temperature` 0.7) with the Action Center system prompt and customer profile.\n\n### Before you run it\n",
          "1. Use self-hosted n8n on this machine. The score step is an Execute Command against this repo. n8n Cloud cannot read these files.\n2. Create the model artifacts if `models/` is empty: `python src/train_model.py`\n3. In **Runtime Config**, set `project_dir`, `python_bin`, and `shell` (`windows` or `linux`).\n4. On **Draft Retention Email**, attach a Header Auth credential whose name is `x-api-key` and whose value is your `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.\n"],
        "height": 460,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c4a1e8b0-7d32-4f61-9a10-0b6e1c2d3001",
      "name": "Pipeline Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
